.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "const char * schultz_result_string (int32_t result)"

.PP
Returns a stable, human readable name for a result code\&. Intended for logging and test output, not for display to end users\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIresult\fP A result code returned by any Schultz function\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A NUL terminated string owned by the library, which must not be freed\&. An unrecognized code yields 'SCHULTZ_ERR_UNKNOWN' rather than NULL, so the return value is always safe to print\&. 
.RE
.PP

